# Features without a "# demo:" group in request-shield.rules, each with the
# reason (0031 F.2; tests/FeatureContractTest.php reads this file): a feature
# that cannot be shown by rows of its own -- PHP, not rules; decided by the page;
# or shown by every row already. Anything else gets a group.
RSF05-02  settings: every line of the demo's rules is one; a group of its own would show nothing new
RSF05-07  the single file: how the shield is installed, not what it decides
RSF06-04  plugins and extensions: PHP classes, not rule lines (the demo's statistics are one)
RSF03-03  the check inside the form: the box solves it while a visitor types, the page reads the answer -- shown as "# try:" rows, decided by no rule an expect line could name
RSF03-04  the site asks for the check: the page decides (requirePass(), X-RS-Check: 1) -- shown as "# try:" rows
RSF05-04  examples next to the rules: every group of the demo is made of them, and request-shield test decides each -- a group of its own would only repeat them
RSF05-05  the log and rule IDs: every row names the rule that decides it, and the front page shows the log -- a group of its own would only repeat them
RSF04-03  the HTTP cache: it keeps the site's answers, and the demo's pages show live counters and the log -- a cached demo would show old ones; its end-to-end test shows it
